hadiths[25]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16326","He said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Hafsah, from al-Rabab al-Dabbiyyah, from Salman ibn 'Amir al-Dabbi, that he said: When one of you breaks his fast, let him break it on dates, and if he does not find, let him break it on water, for water is purifying."
"16327","Hisham said: And 'Asim al-Ahwal narrated to me that Hafsah raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"16328","He said: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Hafsah, from al-Rabab, from her uncle Salman ibn 'Amir al-Dabbi, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Let him break his fast on dates, and if he does not find, let him break his fast on water, for it is purifying."
"16329","And with the boy is his 'aqiqah, so remove harm from him and shed blood on his behalf."
"16330","And charity to the relative is two: charity and kinship."
"16331","He said: Waki' narrated to us, he said: Ibn 'Awn narrated to us, from Hafsah bint Sirin, from al-Rabab bint Sulay', from Salman ibn 'Amir al-Dabbi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Charity to the poor is charity, and it upon the relative is two: kinship and charity."
"16332","He said: Waki' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Asim al-Ahwal, from Hafsah, from al-Rabab Umm al-Raih bint Sulay', from Salman ibn 'Amir al-Dabbi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you breaks his fast, let him break it on dates, and if he does not find, let him break it on water, for it is purifying."
"16333","He said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Ibn Numayr narrated to us, they said: Hisham narrated to us, and Yazid said: Hisham informed us, from Hafsah bint Sirin, from Salman ibn 'Amir al-Dabbi, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Ibn Numayr said: that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Yazid ibn Harun said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: With the boy is his 'aqiqah, so shed blood on his behalf and remove harm from him."
"16334","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from Ibn Sirin, from Salman ibn 'Amir al-Dabbi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: With the boy is his 'aqiqah, so shed blood on his behalf and remove harm from him."
"16335","He said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: 'Asim narrated to us, from Hafsah, from al-Rabab, from Salman ibn 'Amir al-Dabbi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you breaks his fast, let him break it on dates, and if he does not find, let him break it on water, for it is purifying."
"16336","He said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us, from Hafsah bint Sirin, from al-Rabab, from Salman ibn 'Amir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you breaks his fast, let him break it on dates, and if he does not find, let him break it with water, for water is purifying."
"16337","And he said: With the boy is his 'aqiqah, so shed blood on his behalf and remove harm from him."
"16338","And he said: Charity to the poor is charity, and it upon the blood relative is two: kinship and charity."
"16339","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us, from Hafsah, from Salman ibn 'Amir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Charity to the poor is charity, and charity to the blood relative is two: charity and kinship."
"16340","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Hisham, he said: Hafsah narrated to me, from Salman ibn 'Amir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: With the boy is his 'aqiqah, so shed blood on his behalf and remove harm from him."
"16341","He said: And I heard him saying: Your charity to the poor is charity, and it upon the blood relative is two: charity and kinship."
"16342","Muhammad ibn Abi 'Adi narrated to us, from Ibn 'Awn, from Hafsah bint Sirin, from Umm al-Raih bint Sulay', from Salman ibn 'Amir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Charity to the poor is charity, and indeed it upon the blood relative is two: indeed it is charity and kinship."
"16343","'Affan narrated to us: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, he said: Ayyub and Habib and Yunus and Qatadah informed us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Salman ibn 'Amir al-Dabbi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the boy: His 'aqiqah, so shed blood on his behalf and remove harm from him."
"16344","He narrated to us:"
"16345","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Salman ibn 'Amir; Ayyub did not mention the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"16346","And Hisham, from Muhammad, from Salman, raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: For the boy is an 'aqiqah, so shed blood on his behalf and remove harm from him."
"16347","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub and Qatadah, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Salman ibn 'Amir al-Dabbi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the boy: His 'aqiqah, so shed blood on his behalf and remove harm from him."
"16348","He said: Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Ata narrated to us, from Ibn 'Awn and Sa'id, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Salman ibn 'Amir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: With the boy is his 'aqiqah, so shed blood on his behalf and remove harm from him. He said: And Ibn Sirin used to say: If removing harm is not shaving the head, then I do not know what it is."
"16349","He said: 'Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, from Salman ibn 'Amir al-Dabbi, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: With the boy is his 'aqiqah, so shed blood on his behalf and remove harm from him."
"16350","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Hafsah, from Salman ibn 'Amir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Whoever finds dates, let him break his fast on them, and if he does not find dates, let him break his fast on water, for water is purifying."
